L = lesson(ch, "settlement-tourism", "Rural settlement and tourism",
    ["Classify rural settlement patterns and explain their causes", "Describe tourist attractions and the impacts of tourism in Cameroon", "Evaluate tourism management and ecotourism"],
    [("definition", "Settlement patterns", "**Nucleated** settlements have buildings clustered around a centre (a village square, spring, chief’s compound); **dispersed** settlements have scattered farms or compounds; **linear** settlements stretch along a road, river or valley. **Site** is the exact location; **situation** its position relative to surroundings. Factors: water supply, defence, relief and drainage, soils, routes, land tenure and history."),
     ("retenir", "Patterns in Cameroon", "In forest regions, villages often line the roads (linear), partly because roads were built to link them. In the western highlands compounds are often dispersed among farms. In the savanna and Sahel, clusters near water, such as wells and rivers, are common. These are general patterns, with many exceptions."),
     ("retenir", "Tourism", "Attractions include Mount Cameroon, the beaches of Limbe and Kribi, waterfalls, national parks and reserves such as Waza in the north, cultural heritage in places like Foumban, and festivals. **Benefits:** jobs, income, infrastructure, conservation funding. **Costs:** pollution, pressure on land and water, cultural change, benefits leaking abroad, seasonal work. **Ecotourism** aims to conserve nature and benefit local people. Constraints: infrastructure, marketing, security perceptions and cost of travel."),
     ("attention", "Evaluation tip", "In tourism questions give both benefits and costs, name a place, and show who gains and who loses. Avoid sweeping statements like ‘tourism always brings development’.")],
    [("Example 1 — Explain a linear village", "Why might a forest village stretch along a road?",
      ["The road brings access to markets and services.", "Homes near the road are convenient for trading and travel.", "Farmland lies behind the houses on each side."], "Access to the road gives a line of houses."),
     ("Example 2 — Impacts of tourism", "Give one benefit and one cost of tourism at a national park, with who is affected.",
      ["Benefit: guides and lodge workers from nearby villages earn income.", "Cost: more vehicles and waste may disturb animals and ecosystems.", "A fair share of fees can help local people accept conservation."], "Income for locals but environmental pressure; management is needed.")],
    [M("A settlement along a road is", "Linear", ["Nucleated", "Dispersed", "Isolated"], "Houses form a line."),
     TF("Ecotourism aims to protect nature and benefit local communities.", True, "That is its definition."),
     MT("Match each pattern to its likely cause.", [("Nucleated", "Single water source"), ("Linear", "Road or river"), ("Dispersed", "Farms spread over fertile land"), ("Site", "Exact location of the village")], "Typical explanations."),
     M("Which is a possible cost of tourism?", "Pressure on water and waste", ["Fewer visitors", "No jobs", "No roads"], "Large numbers of visitors strain services."),
     O("Explain two factors that influence where a village is sited.", "A reliable water supply is vital for people and animals. Dry, safe land above flood level avoids flooding. Other factors: fertile soils nearby, defence in the past, routes and trade, availability of building materials.", "Two factors (2); explanation (2)."),
     O("Discuss the benefits and problems of tourism for a developing region such as the Mount Cameroon area or a northern national park.", "Benefits: jobs for guides, drivers and hotel staff; income for local business; funds for park management; better roads. Problems: litter, disturbance of wildlife, pressure on water, leakage of profits to outside firms, seasonal income and cultural change. Local control, ecotourism and fair benefit sharing improve outcomes.", "Benefits (2); problems (2); management/judgement (1).")],
    [("Site means", "The exact location of a settlement", ["Its relation to other places", "The number of people", "Its date"], "Not to be confused with situation."),
     ("Dispersed settlement has", "Scattered homes", ["Houses in a tight cluster", "A single street", "No houses"], "Common in highlands."),
     ("Ecotourism is", "Tourism that conserves nature and helps locals", ["Mass tourism only", "Business travel", "Travel by plane only"], "Sustainable tourism."),
     ("Waza is known as", "A national park in northern Cameroon", ["A volcano", "A lake", "A port"], "A savanna wildlife park."),
     ("Leakage in tourism means", "Income going to outside firms", ["Water loss", "Oil spill", "Fewer tourists"], "Profits do not stay local.")],
    (set_fig, "Three rural settlement patterns.", "Dots clustered together for nucleated, dots scattered for dispersed and dots in a row along a line for linear."),
    ["Settlement patterns in Cameroon are generalisations; confirm with the teacher’s local case studies.", "Names of attractions (Mount Cameroon, Limbe, Kribi, Waza, Foumban) are well known; check current status and access."])

